    "turn_idx": 40,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, thanks, Nick. And I understand that you are a student of infectious diseases and disaster management. And unfortunately, that's going to be a skill set that we're going to need as the planet warms. And what I learned listening to scientists over the past years is that a lot of the infectious diseases will spread at a greater rate. due to warmer temperatures. You know, before COVID-19 hit, we were dealing with Zika that came out of the tropics and affected women and their babies, and it was a real surprise that that could be sexually transmitted",
