    "turn_text": "and it is entirely frustrating to to watch kind of the inertia, the inaction in power happy in our state capital and in Washington, DC. But have hope because we are making progress. We have a plan. The stars appear to be aligned. But that's not going to solve everything. We are going to need you to run for office and to go into careers in public service. So my advice is, Use your expertise, become an expert in something, become an advocate, whether it's in your neighborhood on a health issue, on something and begin to build a coalition, whether that's your homeowners association or student group or the League of Women Voters or your environmental organizations locally, build those coalitions, we're coming out of COVID now, we'll be able to be together more directly, that's important. And then be sure you understand what the Hillsborough County Commission does, the Tampa City Council. Those are wonderful places to start. Our state legislature really needs help, getting involved in a campaign for a candidate that shares your values. is also very important and it's a terrific experience for when you launch your own campaign. But you need to have a focus, an issue that drives you, that you're passionate about. And I hope you'll do it. And if you need help, I'm here.",
